{"path": "minidb/api.py", "code": "\"\"\"Public entry point of the `minidb` query engine.\n\n`query` is the only public name here; `minidb/__init__.py` re-exports it together\nwith `QueryError` from `minidb.errors`.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom .engine import execute\nfrom .errors import QueryError\nfrom .parser import parse\nfrom .planner import plan\n\n__all__ = [\"query\"]\n\n\ndef query(sql: str, tables: dict[str, list[dict]]) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Execute `sql` against `tables` and return the result rows.\"\"\"\n    _validate_arguments(sql, tables)\n    try:\n        return execute(plan(parse(sql), tables), tables)\n    except QueryError:\n        raise\n    except RecursionError as exc:\n        raise QueryError(\"query is nested too deeply to evaluate\") from exc\n    except Exception as exc:\n        raise QueryError(f\"internal error while executing query: {type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\") from exc\n\n\ndef _validate_arguments(sql: object, tables: object) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Reject argument shapes that would otherwise surface as TypeError.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(sql, str):\n        raise QueryError(f\"sql must be a string, not {type(sql).__name__}\")\n    if not isinstance(tables, dict):\n        raise QueryError(f\"tables must be a dict of table name to rows, not {type(tables).__name__}\")\n    for name, rows in tables.items():\n        if not isinstance(name, str):\n            raise QueryError(f\"table name must be a string, not {type(name).__name__}\")\n        if not isinstance(rows, list):\n            raise QueryError(f\"table {name!r} must be a list of rows, not {type(rows).__name__}\")\n        for position, row in enumerate(rows):\n            if not isinstance(row, dict):\n                raise QueryError(\n                    f\"row {position} of table {name!r} must be a dict, not {type(row).__name__}\"\n                )\n", "exports": ["query"], "concerns": ["The review comments delivered with this round target minidb/functions.py and minidb/parser.py, not api.py; none of them change this module's contract, so the file is unchanged from round 1 apart from this note.", "Two of those findings matter to api.py's guarantee that no TypeError/AttributeError escapes the public API: parser.parse() reportedly does not wrap unexpected exceptions from tokenize(), and functions.compare() returns None for NULL comparisons, which a careless caller turns into TypeError. api.py already converts every escaping Exception into QueryError, so the public contract holds, but the resulting message will read as an internal error rather than a useful diagnostic until parser and engine wrap at the point of detection.", "The published planner interface guarantees plan.limit/plan.offset are already non-negative and that only QueryError leaves plan(); api.py does not re-check them, per its own published note that it performs no validation beyond argument shapes and the catch-all wrap.", "Argument validation walks every row of every supplied table so a malformed row cannot reach the parser or engine as a TypeError. For very large inputs this is a linear pre-pass, which is the only way to honour the no-TypeError contract without duplicating another module's logic.", "KeyboardInterrupt and SystemExit propagate deliberately: they are BaseException subclasses, not Exception, so `except Exception` leaves them alone."]}
